# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore
# PURPOSE: Prevent unnecessary files from being sent to the Docker daemon.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS FOR MLOps:
#   1. Faster build contexts (doesn't upload multi-gigabyte virtual environments).
#   2. Prevents secret leakage (ignores local .env files).
#   3. Keeps container images clean, secure, and minimal.
# =============================================================================

# Python bytecode & cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.pytest_cache/

# Virtual Environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Git history & repository files
.git/
.gitignore

# Docker config
.dockerignore
Dockerfile*

# Documentation & IDE metadata
*.md
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
